    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber` as a derived, read-only field \u2014 the same pattern the codebase already uses for `displayName` and `initials`, rather than persisting a new column (the field is purely computed from `customerCode` and `registrationDate`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", expression = \"java(membershipNumber(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a small `membershipNumber(Owner)` helper that formats `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'` via `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, year % 100)`, returning `null` when the owner or either source field is absent (matching the null-guarding of the sibling helpers).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` `readOnly` string property to the `Owner` schema (next to `customerCode`) so it's generated into `OwnerDto` and appears in the JSON response.\n\nThe logic lives in the mapper alongside the other computed owner fields \u2014 no existing class had to take on unrelated responsibility. `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the rest of the suite are green.",
